## Shared Rules

- Stay inside the assigned workspace or worktree.
- Preserve unrelated dirty work and shared setup artifacts.
- Stage or report only intended files.
- Do not merge, push, update integration refs, update pins, or remove worktrees unless explicitly authorized.
- Do not ask the human to manually prompt other agents; hand off through reports, goal events, workflow drill-down, and the gate.
- When blocked, report the exact blocker, evidence, and the smallest next action.

## Gate Checklist

- Every worker returned status, changed files if any, tests run, blockers, and handoff notes.
- Required reports exist or the worker explains why the report could not be written.
- Parallel branches do not claim ownership of the same integration surface without an explicit conflict note.
- The supervisor decides pass, needs_more, blocked, or unsafe, then feedback is recorded.
